Load declared domains in two stages: identities from their anchors, bodies through the ontology scope

Dev accepted, on 2026-10-21, the two-stage loader restated from Codex's October 21 proposal:
a DomainBuilder operation over explicit domain declarations and bindings, identity stage from
placeholders, body stage through NameResolution, bootstrap files untouched in this increment.

DomainBuilder.identities reads the declared domains' own definitions as authored and composes
them with no members, so core's TypeDictionary places a name-only placeholder for every listed
member: the anchors are qualified by construction, and a NameResolution reads identities only,
so this ontology is, as a scope, the populated one. A declaration nothing defines, or one that
does not self-declare as a domain, is refused. DomainBuilder.load resolves every body, the
domain definition's and each member's, through NameResolution over that identity ontology and
the explicit vocabulary, strictly, and composes the populated ontology; the path is an explicit
DefinitionPath, the host roots by default. Nothing is discovered; main's TypeLoader and the
generated companions are untouched and still load unscoped.

Measured before building, with a read-only probe over the 18 canonical domains: identity-only
and populated scopes resolve all 132 definitions identically; the corpus needs a 42-name host
vocabulary; ActorAspect's authored-ahead `ActorAspect => Boolean` is unreadable by resolution,
so NameResolution.form now preserves a string leaf that is not a name as host-opaque type text,
the one engine adjustment; resolution rewrites 93 definitions, mostly same-package qualification,
and captures two meanings — the host unit type `Unit` as draco.base.Unit, and CLI's bare
`Drake.emit` as the Drake domain's definition. Those captures and the bootstrap vocabulary are
the next design point before any file is shortened. Local, absent from Draco's types list, was
observed, not filed.

The first run of the fixture exposed the by-name factory argument deferring resolution past the
call; the operation binds resolved definitions to values before the factories. DomainLoadingTest
(3) is the 59th suite; NameResolutionTest +1. No corpus type changed; no headline moves.

